 "summary": "A small through-hole power relay with a single pole and a single contact of cadmium-free silver alloy, built as SPST-NO (1a, four pins) or SPDT (1c, five pins) in a 20.3 × 10.3 × 15.8 mm maximum case. The standard type switches 10 A at 125 VAC on its NO contact and the -EU high-capacity type 10 A at 250 VAC; every type is limited to 277 VAC and 30 VDC. The coil takes about 200 mW (1a) or 400 mW (1c), has class F insulation, and withstands 8 kV impulse and 4,000 VAC against the contacts. Variants add a sealed case (4), IEC/EN 60335-1 home-appliance approval (-HA) and PWM or reduced-voltage holding (-PW). The G5Q-1A4 DC12 is the sealed standard SPST-NO type with a 12 VDC coil of 720 Ω drawing 16.7 mA.",
