   "description": "A low-side N-channel MOSFET switches the relay coil from the supply rail at the full rated coil voltage, its gate driven by a pulse train. A surge absorption diode sits across the coil, cathode to the supply. The validation conditions are a duty of 50% or more at 10 kHz or more, with a diode forward voltage of 0.4 V or less, after the rated voltage has been applied for at least 100 ms to pull the relay in.",
